solution.text:
Total number of 5-digit numbers having all the digits distinct $={ }^{10} \mathrm{P}_{5}-{ }^{9} \mathrm{P}_{4}$
$$
\begin{array}{l}
=\frac{10 !}{5 !}-\frac{91}{5 !}=\frac{10 \times 9 !}{5 !}-\frac{91}{51} \\
=\frac{91}{51}(10-1)=9 \times \frac{9!}{(9-4) !} \\
=9 \times 9 P_{4}
\end{array}
$$
